# The step of norm_upper_2 (milestone2.md, "sum, dot, axpy, convolution": norm_upper_k): the step
# of one limb on the leading limb of the element. A normalized pair is strictly between the
# neighbors of its leading limb (normalized_2_between, proofs/theories/Convert.v), so the step
# after the largest magnitude of a leading limb bounds every element: the finish takes it once.
kernel:        norm_step_2
input:         m
input:         mask ok
input:         x = x0 x1
output:        r
output:        mask okr
requires:      normalized x
ensures:       maximum r m abs(x[0])
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/FoldNorm.v norm_step_2_correct
source:        the larger of the state and the magnitude of the leading limb (milestone2.md, norm_upper_k)
license:       proof: MIT
status:        proved
unused:        x1 the second limb of a normalized pair is within the neighbors of the first; the finish's one step covers it
cone_exempt:   a maximum is a select after a comparison (norm_combine); a NaN leading limb is kept in the mask okr, and an infinite one in r, which the finish of the fold tests

(r, okr) = norm_step_1(m, ok, x0)
